 "text": "Hey there, how are you? Make sure the house is familiar, avoid new places until he's settled. Keep routines as much as possible, they help. Short clear explanations help. He may not remember anything else. Explain where everything is, who people are, and where you are in building. A sticker chart of the floors helps him keep track. Yes, small ones can be wonderful. A zoo visit can be exciting without being overwhelming. Try not to take it personally. Your dad might say things out of confusion, not anger. And ask him kindly so he doesn't feel hurt.",
